{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "10207f0e-64ca-8c0a-9f3a-e373732d2f91",
  "created_at": "2026-01-14T12:29:48-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Zoning and Inspections",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Tony Pellegrino",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Greg Lombardi",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T12:24:55-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Zoning and Inspections, this is Greg."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T12:24:58-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hello, good afternoon. Yes, my name is Tony Pellegrino. I am calling about a fence. I am sorry, I am on the speaker, my hands are full."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T12:25:09-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's fine, I can hear you. What's the question on the fence?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T12:25:14-05:00",
      "duration": 18,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "So I have a quote from a fence company. I have not signed yet. I want to check first, before I sign anything, if I need a permit for this. Or is it only a call to the city? I do not understand which one it is."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T12:25:32-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. What kind of fence, and how tall?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T12:25:36-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It is composite. Not wood. The company says about four and a half feet tall. Four and a half, yes."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T12:25:44-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "And where's the property?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T12:25:46-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "478 Carroll Avenue. It is a rental, I am the landlord. The back yard and one side."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T12:25:53-05:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Alright. In general, a fence usually does need a permit here, it's not just a courtesy call. The height and where it sits on the lot are what we look at. Four and a half feet is something we'd want to see on paper first."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T12:26:10-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Ah, so it is a permit. Not only a call. I thought maybe under five feet, no permit. This is what the man told me."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T12:26:20-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Contractors say a lot of things. Don't count on that. Who's pulling it, you or the fence company?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T12:26:28-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sorry, who is pulling what?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T12:26:31-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "The permit. Either you apply as the owner, or the company applies for you. Plenty of them do it, so ask them before you sign. Make sure it's written in the contract who does it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T12:26:45-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, okay. I ask them, who applies. And if they do it, I still sign something? Or only them?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T12:26:53-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Usually the owner signs off on the application, yes. If you're the owner of record, that's you."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T12:27:00-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, I am the owner. [pause] Another question. How close to the property line can I put it? The company says one foot from the line. Is that correct? Or it can be on the line?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T12:27:14-05:00",
      "duration": 20,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I wouldn't take either of those from the contractor. Setbacks depend on the zone and the fence type, and you do not want to guess, because if it ends up on the neighbor's side you're tearing it out. When you apply, they'll want a plot plan or a survey showing where it goes."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T12:27:34-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "A survey. I do not have a survey. I have, um, the deed papers only."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T12:27:41-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "The deed might help, but a plot plan is better. If you don't have a survey, bring what you've got and the staff here can tell you if it's enough. Come by the office or send it in."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T12:27:56-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. So I bring the deed, the quote from the company, and I write the height, four and a half feet, composite. And where it goes on a drawing."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T12:28:08-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's a good start. A simple sketch with distances to the lot lines is fine to begin with."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T12:28:16-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "[line breaks up] ...sorry, I lost you. A sketch with what?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T12:28:21-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "A sketch, with the distances from the fence to each property line. Measure it out."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T12:28:27-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, yes, measurements. I write it down. I keep all the spending in a spiral notebook, every repair, every bill for the house. So the permit goes in the notebook also. Do you know how much it costs, the permit?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T12:28:43-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "The fee depends on the project, and I don't want to throw out a number that's wrong. The front counter will give you the exact amount when you hand in the application."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T12:28:56-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, okay. And how long does it take, until I can start?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T12:29:01-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It varies. Don't schedule the fence company until you have the permit in hand. That's the main thing."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T12:29:09-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "So, do not sign yet. First ask the company who applies. Then bring the papers. Then permit. Then the fence. Yes?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T12:29:18-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You can sign the contract if it says the work starts after the permit. But yes, that's the order."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T12:29:26-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Ah, that is different. Okay. Contract says after permit. I understand now. Mostly."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T12:29:32-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "If anything's unclear, call us back or stop in. We're open until the end of the afternoon."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T12:29:39-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thank you, Greg, very much. You helped me a lot. God bless you and your family."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T12:29:46-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You too. Take care."
    }
  ],
